course: dictionary
lesson: 10406
title: Tricky: hard, and clever at tricking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tricky has two meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. The first meaning is difficult and needing care or skill: «Some things are tricky: toothpaste, ketchup and cornflour slime behave like a solid one moment and a liquid the next.» Here tricky means hard to predict, because the stuff keeps changing.
explain: The second meaning is about people. A tricky person is clever at tricking or deceiving others. Tricky people can be adults or strangers who try to get children to go with them or keep secrets. If that happens, say no, get away, and tell a safe adult straight away.
explain: At school, «tricky words» are words that cannot easily be sounded out, like «said» and «the». Many are old words whose sound changed while the spelling stayed the same. «A tricky word is almost never tricky all the way through», so look for the one bit that is hard and focus on that.
fact: Tricky means difficult and needing care or skill.
fact: «A tricky question» is one that needs careful thought before you answer.
fact: A tricky person is clever at tricking or deceiving others.
fact: «Tricky words» are words that cannot easily be sounded out, like «said» and «the».
fact: If someone tries to trick you into going with them or keeping a secret, say no, get away and tell a safe adult.
exercise: Mia says, «This is a tricky question.» What does tricky mean here? | Clean and bright | Very funny and silly | Sweet to taste | *Difficult and needing care or skill
exercise: What are «tricky words» at school? | Words that rhyme with each other | Words that are always written in capitals | Words with only one letter | *Words that cannot easily be sounded out, like «said»
exercise: «A tricky word is almost never tricky all the way through.» What does this suggest? | Every letter of a tricky word is hard | Tricky words are never found in books | *Usually only one part of the word is hard | Tricky words are always very long
test: A tricky person is best described as | Always on time for school | Kind and helpful to everyone | *Clever at tricking or deceiving others
test: A stranger tries to get you to go with them. What should you do? | *Say no, get away and tell a safe adult | Go with them to be polite | Keep it a secret from everyone | Wait and see what happens
exam: «Some things are tricky: toothpaste, ketchup and cornflour slime behave like a solid one moment and a liquid the next.» Which meaning of tricky fits? | Clever at tricking people | Tasty and sweet | Lost in the dark | *Difficult to understand or predict
